# ---- Build / packaging artefacts -------------------------------------------------
workled.zip

# ---- JavaScript package managers: all local caches / state files ----------------
# node_modules is purely the output of `pnpm install / npm install` and can be
# regenerated at any time; never commit it (it would be hundreds of MBs of
# third-party binary blobs that differ per OS / Node ABI).
node_modules/

# pnpm writes a family of dotfile caches under the `.pnpm*` prefix on every
# install/update run. None of these are source-controlled inputs:
#   - .pnpm-workspace-state-v1.json – dependency graph snapshot of a workspace
#     (pnpm 9+); machine-specific, path-encoded, stale after any dep change.
#   - .pnpm-store                – content-addressable mirror of the store;
#     absolute-path sensitive and OS/Node-ABI locked.
#   - .pnpmfile-local.cjs / etc  – local-only overrides (users keep those
#     private; never share them in a skill repo).
# We explicitly RE-ALLOW the two source-controlled pnpm files so a future
# maintainer can opt this skill into a monorepo workspace without editing
# .gitignore again:
.pnpm*
!.pnpmfile.cjs
!pnpm-workspace.yaml

# ---- pnpm-lock.yaml -------------------------------------------------------------
# This skill declares ZERO npm dependencies (see package.json: there are no
# `dependencies` or `devDependencies` fields). A generated lockfile is
# therefore only pnpm boilerplate (lockfileVersion + `importers: .: {}`), with
# nothing to pin. Keeping the empty boilerplate misleads future maintainers
# into thinking `pnpm install` is required here, so we keep it out of git.
#
# If the skill ever grows a real dependency (e.g. you add `@abandonware/noble`
# for native GATT), delete the line below and re-commit the generated
# pnpm-lock.yaml together with the new dependency list in package.json.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# ---- npm / yarn garbage (defence-in-depth, harmless if unused) ----------------
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
